First thoughts coming out of Christopher Nolan's epic The Odyssey:
- See it in the largest format you can. IMAX was worth the price of admission;
- The first act was a little rough. I expected Nolan to do his non-linear routine to smooth out some of the sluggishness, but he didn't really do so (1/x)

THE ODYSSEY (2026): Yes, the story has been translated and adapted in all forms of media, and yet Christopher Nolan has found a way to give it new life once more. This is an epic of the highest order. My review.
